Stashing.(DS: stack)
    Both staged and unstaged changes(if they are being tracked) can be stashed.

With Stash                              Without Stash

git add .
Stash your current changes              Stage your current changes.
Pull the latest change                  Commit them.
Pop the stash                           Pull the latest changes.
Continue working                        Continue and finish your feature.
Finish your feature                     Create another commit.
                                        Squash all the commits.

git stash
    Output sample: Saved working directory and index state WIP on feature: b9f9a6e Done fixing header

git stash list (stash@{n})
git stash list -p (Show the changes that have been stashed)

git stash show (Show all the files that have been stashed with +, - data)

git stash pop - Apply and remove from the stash.
git stash apply [stash@{n}] - Apply without removing the entry from the stash
git stash drop [stash@{n}] - Don't apply, just remove from the stash


